==============================================================================
single_limit=180, two_swap_limit=36, alias_depth=4, lcm_tail_max=5, qmax=64, q27_m=27
[0] Assumption challenge
  considered vertices:
    runners, gaps, safe components, endpoint owners, residue classes,
    denominators, rational twists, blocked twist events, speed blockers,
    divisor fibers, source-spectrum nodes, and proof obligations.
  chosen vertices:
    rational twists a/q and the speed-vs-twist blocker hypergraph.
  preserved LRC predicate:
    if any selected twist has ||v*a/q|| >= 1/14 for every speed v,
    it is an exact LRC14 certificate for that row.
  destroyed information:
    open intervals between selected twists and fine endpoint ownership.
  challenged assumption:
    the proof need not start from boundary gaps; it can start from a
    global primal witness ladder and read failed ladders as dual covers.

